[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4612996733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4612996733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4612996733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEvS-fQ","user":{"login":"TariqAfandi","id":189516872,"node_id":"U_kgDOC0vMSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189516872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi","html_url":"https://github.com/TariqAfandi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T13:46:14Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T13:46:14Z","body":"After looking into this, I noticed the behavior breaks in two ways depending on the weights:\n\n- If the negative weight's absolute value equals the sum of the others (e.g. `[1.0, 2.0, 3.0, -6.0]`), the total sum is `0.0` and the function always returns index `0`.\n- If the sum doesn't hit zero but is still skewed, the distribution is silently wrong with no indication to the developer.\n\nNegative weights don't really make sense for weighted random selection since they represent negative probability, so I think catching them at input would be the cleanest fix, which seems to line up with what was discussed in #119948. Something like:\n\n```cpp\nfor (int64_t i = 0; i < weights_size; ++i) {\n    if (weights[i] < 0.0) {\n        ERR_PRINT(\"rand_weighted: weight at index \" + itos(i) + \" is negative, treating as 0.\");\n        continue;\n    }\n    weights_sum += weights[i];\n}\n```\n\nThis way invalid input is caught early and the developer gets a clear message. Happy to open a PR for this if it seems like the right direction, though I'm open to feedback since this would be my first contribution.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4612996733/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613139118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4613139118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4613139118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEvbqrg","user":{"login":"PodunkGames","id":286503757,"node_id":"U_kgDOEROzTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286503757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames","html_url":"https://github.com/PodunkGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T14:00:08Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T14:00:08Z","body":"I'm not sure if a warning or error is more appropriate for this type of thing. (the documentation PR I initially opened for this #119948 was also my first contribution) I agree that it's the right course of action though to catch it.\nMight say more about me than about the engine, but in my personal run-in with this issue I was expecting the negative values to act like zero and wrote my dynamic loot tables as-such. The idea being that negative numbers would provide an offset that a luck stat would need to improve before it would breach zero and become possible to get Legendary-tier loot. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613139118/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613261072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4613261072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4613261072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEvjHEA","user":{"login":"TariqAfandi","id":189516872,"node_id":"U_kgDOC0vMSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189516872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi","html_url":"https://github.com/TariqAfandi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TariqAfandi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T14:11:59Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T14:11:59Z","body":"That's a good point. If someone is intentionally using negative weights as an offset mechanic, clamping to zero would silently break that without any indication. \n\nMaybe the better approach is `WARN_PRINT` instead of `ERR_PRINT`, without modifying the values at all:\n\n```cpp\nif (weights[i] < 0.0) {\n    WARN_PRINT(\"rand_weighted: weight at index \" + itos(i) + \" is negative.\");\n}\nweights_sum += weights[i];\n```\n\nThat way accidental negative weights get flagged visibly, intentional use cases like yours still work exactly as before, and no behavior is silently altered. The developer sees the warning and can decide whether it's a mistake or intentional.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613261072/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613375235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4613375235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4613375235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEvqFAw","user":{"login":"PodunkGames","id":286503757,"node_id":"U_kgDOEROzTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286503757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames","html_url":"https://github.com/PodunkGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T14:23:17Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T14:23:17Z","body":"> intentional use cases like yours still work exactly as before, and no behavior is silently altered.\n\nTo be clear, my use case DOESN'T work, that's just how I was hoping to use it. 😅 So I'm at no risk of a breaking change here, as it's already broken. \nMy ideal resolution for this issue so it would work within my personal (but wrong) initial interpretation is that negative weights are treated entirely like zero. They aren't added to the sum, make no difference in the repeated subtraction, and if all weights are below zero, return `-1`.\n\nI'm just not sure if what's helpful for me is what's best for the whole user base. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613375235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613382253","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4613382253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4613382253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEvqgbQ","user":{"login":"Cyklon3000","id":67823272,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODIzMjcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67823272?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000","html_url":"https://github.com/Cyklon3000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T14:23:59Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T14:23:59Z","body":"I agree.\nUse of this functions with `weights[i] < 0`, indicates that the user misunderstood how it's meant to work (the weights representing relative probabilities). Throwing an error or at least warning is better than post-processing the inputs in a manner that would have to be agreed upon.\nI'd prefer an error thrown as opposed to a warning, since any negative weight _breaks_ the function. To know what it returns you'd have to know how rand_weighted is implemented as there couldn't be a coherent explanation in the docs as to what `rand_weighted` does with negative weights. \nI'd add a line in the docs, that every `weights[i]` has to be `>= 0` otherwise an error is thrown. With something akin to @TariqAfandi suggestion for an implementation in the function but instead of a warning with an error.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4613382253/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4616383486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4616383486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4616383486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEyhr_g","user":{"login":"Cyklon3000","id":67823272,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODIzMjcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67823272?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000","html_url":"https://github.com/Cyklon3000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cyklon3000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T20:20:43Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T20:20:43Z","body":"I'd be willing to implement the fix if no one else already started.\nI would go ahead with the suggestion I provided above (`ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG` and mention in docs) if that's the consensus we've reached.\nApproval from a maintainer would be awesome though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4616383486/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4616452148","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119974#issuecomment-4616452148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119974","id":4616452148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEyl4NA","user":{"login":"PodunkGames","id":286503757,"node_id":"U_kgDOEROzTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286503757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames","html_url":"https://github.com/PodunkGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PodunkGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T20:30:21Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T20:30:21Z","body":"I haven't started anything myself, so by all means. Agreed it would be good to get input from a maintainer ahead of time, but getting something on a PR would probably jumpstart that conversation.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4616452148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]